-- lib/decode.cub — a byte decoder whose access proofs are certificates checked by evaluation
-- (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.2 “B12 — Representations as a construct”, part 3 “Primitives (`lib/prim.cub`, new)”, with F32 of §18.13 “F31–F32 — Reflection and certificates”). Loaded after lib/prim.cub and lib/linproof.cub. load32 n b off needs
-- le (plus off 4) n; a decoder reading a 4-byte field and an 8-byte field at i, given that
-- plus i 8 ≤ n, owes le (plus i 4) n. The obligation is linear arithmetic: it is stated as codes
-- over words (lib/linproof.cub's fragment), the certificate is the multiplier list (1), and
-- cert-sound turns the check's `true` — one evaluation — into the proof, carried across Word ≃ Nat.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- Nat ↔ Word order
congw2 : (f : Nat → Word) → {a b : Nat} → a ≡ b → f a ≡ f b
congw2 f p = λ i → f (p i)
